{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/531551-pimp-my-concept-the-three","id":531551,"title":"Pimp my concept: the Three.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-28T19:36:24-07:00","id":531551,"title":"Pimp my concept: the Three.","content":"Basic premise: Emily, single 30-year-old mother of 10-year-old Karen, is abducted by the fae. After a few months in captivity, she returns to find that twenty years have passed, and her daughter is now a 30-year-old cop who's taking care of her \u201cmother\u201d, Emily's 50-year-old fetch. <br /> <br /> All three of these characters are intended to be potential player characters; and the relationships among the three are supposed to be messy: each relationship should allow for common goals as well as opposition, as the desired game is intended to be a horror-tinged interpersonal drama. The basic arrangement is that Emily and her fetch hate each other, but they both care for Karen; and Karen cares for both of them but doesn't trust either one. They <i>should</i> be able to pull together in the face of a greater threat; but <i>can</i> they? <br /> <br /> I want Emily to be socially oriented: pledges should be a big thing for her, and I want her to have a Kith and Contracts that promote social networking. I <i>think</i> that Fairest is the most appropriate Seeming for her; but I\u2019m not sure. Her fetch is an \u201colder and wiser\u201d (and more twisted) version of her who has had twenty years of experience that Emily lacks, but lacks Emily and Karen's youth. Karen is in many ways her mother's daughter; people who can't see through Emily's Mask often mistake them for twins. But Karen is much more physically active; she's gone from tomboy to cop by day, Hedge explorer by night. When things get violent, she's the most effective of the trio. <br /> <br /> That's as much as I've got so far. What would you do with the concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:24:57-07:00","id":531636,"title":"","content":"Given the Maiden-Mother-Crone set-up that you've got going on, I can easily see supernatural elements weighing in, but I'd need to know more about Emily/Fetch-ily's life experiences before coming up with anything more concrete. What was Emily's life like before her Durance? Was Fetch-ily aware that she was a fetch, or did it all come to her after meeting Emily? Or is she still convinced that she's Karen's mother, no matter what this stranger says? And how does Karen react when she suddenly finds out that she &quot;has two mommies&quot;? As a cop, has she had any horrifying experiences to draw on, supernatural or otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:50:44-07:00","id":531679,"title":"","content":"I'm toying around with Karen being fae-touched, in the new sense of the term: she was drawn into the Hedge by dreams of her mother\u2019s Durance; and when she came back, she could see the fae for what they are. Including her \u201cmom\u201d. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the fetch didn\u2019t realize that she was a fetch until Karen confronted her, making for a heart-wrenching discovery of her own true nature. I\u2019m figuring that the \u201creveal\u201d took place later rather than sooner, possibly as recently as the end of Emily\u2019s Durance. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I\u2019m debating the possibility of tying the end of Emily\u2019s Durance into Karen\u2019s first foray into the Hedge \u2014 though I\u2019m not sure if I want to say that Karen directly helped Emily escape. I keep thinking that I want Karen and the fetch to have their confrontation before Emily shows up. <br /> <br /> As for what Emily\u2019s life was like before her Durance, I don't know much more than I've already said: single mother raising a daughter. And something that's suitable to both her own social focus and her fetch's eventual mental focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T21:30:35-07:00","id":531707,"title":"","content":"I like this concept a lot. Fetches have always been one of my favorite things about CtL, and I love exploring the different ways a Changeling can deal with them. Lots of dramatic potential!<br /> <br /> Not sure if Fairest is best. It is the optimal Seeming for a social character, but that doesn't mean you can't make a great social character of another Seeming. Need to know more about the character to say what would work best. I'd actually lean away from Fairest, because I wouldn't want her Seeming to make it easier to win her daughter's trust and affection.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Emily resents the 20 years of experiences that her daughter and Fetch share, so I imagine she'll jump at any opportunity to remind Karen of fond memories from before her abduction or to forge new memories. So bringing up objects or events from before the abduction or new life events and experiences that Emily can try to be a major part of (possibly while blocking the Fetches involvement), like a wedding or a new house or celebrating a big promotion, will be a great tool for exploring their relationship. <br /> <br /> I would think that Karen would probably treat the Fetch more like her mother, while treating Emily more like a contemporary (since she's basically a stranger and is nearly the same age). Meaning that Karen is more likely to accept advice or being maternally protective from the Fetch than from Emily. She might get annoyed with life advice or overprotective behavior from someone who doesn't know her very well and isn't any more worldly and experienced (and is also 20 years out of touch with society). I'm sure this will really chafe Emily and probably lend the Fetch some smug satisfaction. So try to engineer plot where Karen needs protection or help or advice and the Fetch and mother can compete. <br /> <br /> I'd tempt both the Fetch and Emily with ways to get rid of the other. The Fetch could hand Emily back to her Keeper; Emily could have the local Freehold &quot;take care&quot; of the Fetch. Neither will take advantage because it would ruin their relationship with Karen if she found out, but it should be an ever present and extremely attractive option.<br /> <br /> Put Karen in positions where she is forced to choose between trusting one or the other. Maybe Emily hears a rumor in the Freehold, but it's contradicted by a dream the Fetch has that may be prophetic. Maybe Emily is prevented from telling her daughter something by a pledge, and the Fetch finds out that she's keeping secrets. Also, try to put Karen in spots where she must choose between potentially harming one &quot;mom&quot; or the other. You-can-only-save-one-type situations (though probably not life and death). Karen can prevent the Fetch from losing her house to eminent domain, but it will cause Emily to fail to uphold a pledge to a local politician, for example. Both of these tactics should be used sparingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T23:10:33-07:00","id":531751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/531551-pimp-my-concept-the-three?p=531707#post531707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this concept a lot. Fetches have always been one of my favorite things about CtL, and I love exploring the different ways a Changeling can deal with them. Lots of dramatic potential!<br /> <br /> Not sure if Fairest is best. It is the optimal Seeming for a social character, but that doesn't mean you can't make a great social character of another Seeming. Need to know more about the character to say what would work best. I'd actually lean away from Fairest, because I wouldn't want her Seeming to make it easier to win her daughter's trust and affection.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way that a Seeming makes it easier for a changeling to do stuff is that it influences what her Contracts can do. Now, does Emily <i>really</i> want to earn back Karen's trust and affection by <i>using faerie magic to mess with her mind?</i> You mentioned later on putting temptations before Emily and her fetch, though you were thinking in terms of temptations to get rid of each other; well, this is the same sort of thing: why not just reach out and <i>make</i> her trust you? It would be so easy\u2026<br /> <br /> Still, I'm open to considering other Seemings for Emily. Of course, the fact that we've only seen three so far is a bit of a problem there. There's also the fact that, as a fae-touched, Karen should also have a Seeming. I'm willing to bet that 2e fetches <i>don't</i> get Seemings; but I wonder if they get Kiths? Oh well; it's just speculation for now. <br /> <br /> I've read the rest of your advice; and on a first pass, it all looks good; I'll need to chew on it a bit, though. <br /> <br /> Still open to further advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T00:03:20-07:00","id":531763,"title":"","content":"I was referring to the way the flavor text describes the Fairest. Under Appearance in the draft it says that &quot;When she speaks, it\u2019s easy to believe her...&quot; and &quot;Whatever she does, the Fairest duty and responsibility peek through, and so when someone is in trouble. Without consideration, it\u2019s the Fairest\u2019s feet they will throw themselves down on. &quot; Maybe I'm just reading too much into the fluff, but to me that read like a passive effect that may not have a mechanics, but is intended to inform the way interactions with the Fairest are role played.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Contracts being an additional temptation. Certainly a powerful violation of trust if she were to use them on Karen. Reminds me of Willow using magic to make Tara forget arguments in Buffy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T22:40:49-07:00","id":546518,"title":"","content":"There is a lot of story potential in Karen being the cop aware of the supernatural, while Emily is part of a population that lives outside the law. Lots of opportunity for conflict and Dresden style detective stories. Ironically the fetch is the one rooted in the mundane world and given the social to mental path you describe may hold a position of influence in that world, perhaps government or the media, and more than anything she seeks to keep her daughter safely wrapped up in the banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:48:32-07:00","id":548092,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. Yeah, it definitely makes sense for Emily-2 to have a bunch of ties to the community \u2014 make her rich and influential, perhaps a public figure of some sort. Since she's supposed to be a potential protagonist, it shouldn't <i>all</i> be about power and influence for her; perhaps she funds (or runs) a local charity, or is held in high esteem in the community because of some great service she performed in the past: she has clout because she's <i>earned</i> it\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T08:25:02-07:00","id":576384,"title":"","content":"Given that I have now seen all of the Seemings, I'm leaning heavily in favor of Emily being Wizened, with her chosen craft having a strong social aspect to it. An antiques dealer, maybe\u2026<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about Karen's Seeming, though. Given that she's intended to be the \u201ccombat monster\u201d of the group, Ogre might be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-02-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T20:54:06-07:00","id":578122,"title":"","content":"I would base Karen's seeming upon what kind of cop she is; do her suspects often 'resist arrest', does she excel at undercover work or heavily use informants, or is she more of a profiler who understands her prey? Any of the seemings can be used to create a 'combat monster', if ones who use different weapons and methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}